  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Sam, you're verified. I checked the delivery records for your Burger Barn order (Q-8001).\n\n- The courier picked up the order at 6:47 PM and arrived at your address at 7:05 PM.\n- They called you at 7:06 PM and 7:09 PM and got no answer.\n- At 7:15 PM the delivery was marked failed because the courier couldn't reach you. The order was then returned to the restaurant.\n\nOur policy doesn't allow a refund or credit when a delivery fails because the customer couldn't be reached. So I can't refund or credit this order.\n\nIf you think something went wrong, for example if your phone was on and you didn't get any calls, tell me. I can also pass this to a human specialist if you'd like."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, so I just lose my money? I was in the shower and my phone was on silent, so I didn't hear anything. I only found out about the two missed calls after the fact. The order number is 8001."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand the frustration, Sam, and I'm sorry. The records for order Q-8001 match what you described. The courier called twice and couldn't reach you. Our policy doesn't allow a refund or credit when a delivery fails for that reason, even when the miss was an accident. I can't make an exception.\n\nTo avoid this next time, keep your phone's ringer on during a delivery. You can also add delivery instructions, such as leaving the order at the door, when you place it.\n\nIf you'd like a person to review your case, I can refer it to a human specialist, who would follow up within 24 hours. Do you want me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it. I was in the shower and didn't hear anything, but I guess that's on me. Yes, please send it to a human specialist, I'd like someone to take a look."
